<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name    "unraid-swiss-manager">
<!ENTITY author  "Stiphr">
<!ENTITY version "2026.10.28b1">
<!ENTITY emhttp  "/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY flash   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Stiphr/Unraid-Swiss-Manager/refs/heads/beta/unraid-swiss-manager.plg">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" launch="Settings/UnraidSwissManager" min="6.9.0" icon="unraid-swiss-manager.png">

<CHANGES>
###2026.10.28b1
- BETA. Renamed: the plugin file is now unraid-swiss-manager.plg (it was unraid-autoupdater.plg). Update the old entry on the Plugins page once: it installs Unraid Swiss Manager from the beta branch, carries over settings, history, webhook and backups, and removes itself. Version numbers start again at 2026.10.28 under the new name.
- BETA. New Dashboard tile: a status dot and summary, one clean row per item (only when it has something to say), and a single line with the last and next run. Each row opens its tab. Fixes labels running into their values on Unraid 7.
- BETA. Settings page: ?tab=docker|plugins|os|cleanup|backups|settings|activity opens that tab directly.
###2026.11.02b1
- BETA. New: Backups tab, appdata: "Stop the containers while the backup runs" (off by default). Running containers that use the appdata folders are stopped for the backup and started again afterwards in their "update after" order, also when the backup fails, so databases are captured consistently. A container that does not come back is reported as a failed backup.
- BETA. Fix: a per-container safety backup that failed halfway no longer pushes the oldest good backup out; image and appdata parts are written under a temporary name first.
- BETA. Fix: scheduled appdata backups no longer include the Cleanup quarantine folder.
- BETA. Fix (Unraid 6.9 / PHP 7.4): after a plugin update check, saved container templates could not be read, so Cleanup did not warn about folders a saved template still uses and listed no saved templates.
- BETA. Improved: an automatic reboot after an OS update also waits while the mover is running.
- BETA. Improved: no deprecation warnings on newer PHP versions.
###2026.10.31b7
- BETA. The plugin's web address is now Settings/UnraidSwissManager (it was Settings/UnraidAutoUpdater). Links in notifications, Discord messages and the Dashboard tile use it. The old page file is removed on update; an old bookmark needs updating.
###2026.10.31b6
- BETA. Fix: b5 did not include one of its files, so the plugin showed an error (500) after updating. Update again to get it.
###2026.10.31b5
- BETA. New Backups tab: back up your appdata folders and the boot drive (USB flash) to a folder you choose.
- Appdata: weekly or monthly, and optionally right before updates are installed (only when there is something to install; you can choose to hold the updates back if that backup fails). Folders can be left out.
- Boot drive: weekly or monthly, checked after it is written.
- Keep 1, 2 or 3 backups. Older ones are deleted only after a new backup has finished, the newest is never deleted, and a failed backup deletes nothing.
- Each archive is a normal tar.gz, written privately and moved into place only when complete. Results appear in Activity and can notify you.
###2026.10.31b4
- The stable branch is now called stable (it was main). The Stable channel in Settings uses it; old links keep working.
- Renamed: the plugin and its repository are now called Unraid Swiss Manager, with a new logo. Nothing else changes: same settings, same schedule, and the plugin keeps its install name, so existing installs update normally.
- UI refresh (beta). Cleanup tab: Scan, Review, Clean steps; one "Scan for Cleanup Items" button; category cards; each item shows why it is listed and a status (Eligible, Review first, Protected, In use); "Select all eligible" never picks Review first or protected items; Preview (dry run); confirmation lists what can and cannot be undone; results show cleaned, skipped and failed.
- Fixed unreadable badges such as "Skipped: stopped" (Unraid page style leaked into them) with measured AA contrast in all themes; badges also carry an icon, not only a colour.
- Dashboard tile: uses the plugin logo at the right size, no longer shows the Unraid OS version, and shows updates, failures, last check and next run.
- BETA. Settings > very bottom: choose the plugin branch (Stable or Beta) with a warning when Beta is picked, and a Force update that reinstalls the current branch.
- Save settings to a file with a name of your choice (default Unraid-AutoUpdater-Settings-YYYY-MM-DD) and load them back from a file, with a summary before they are applied.
###2026.10.31b3
- BETA. Cleanup tab improved: one "Scan everything" button with a total of what can be freed, folding sections (empty ones start folded), a badge on the tab, and a "Recent cleanups" list (also in Activity).
- Appdata: "Contents" shows what is inside a folder, "Never offer" keeps a folder off the list, folders changed in the last 30 days are flagged, and quick selections (all, not changed for 6 months).
- Optional: delete quarantined folders after N days, and a weekly report (Discord / Unraid notification) of what could be freed. Both are off by default; the report never removes anything.
- Unused Docker volumes can now be reviewed and removed (never forced) next to images and containers.
###2026.10.31b2
- BETA. Cleanup tab now has four parts: Appdata folders, Quarantine, Images and containers, Saved templates.
- Appdata folders: finds folders in your appdata share that no container (running or stopped) uses, with size, age and a preview. Safe mode (default) moves them to a hidden quarantine folder; deleting for good needs Safe mode off and a confirmation. Symbolic links, separate mount points and folders any container maps are never offered.
- Quarantine: restore (never overwrites; offers a "-restored" name when the place is taken) or delete for good.
- Saved templates: archive the saved template of a removed container with a verified backup, and restore it later.
- New Settings > Cleanup (appdata): which folders to check and Safe mode.
###2026.10.31b1
- BETA. Dependency order: containers can be set to update after others (database before app); a dependant is skipped if its dependency failed.
- Skip this version for a container, plugin or the OS release; it comes back with the next version.
- Discord action links (Update now / Skip) straight from the notification; set the web GUI address in Settings.
- Quiet hours: non-urgent notifications are held and sent after the window (failures and rollbacks can still go out).
- Update statistics over time: 30-day chart, most active and most failing.
- Dashboard tile with the number of waiting updates (can be turned off in Appearance).
- One-click rollback for containers to the previous image; the container is pinned and that version skipped until you unpin.
- Major-version guard for selected containers (e.g. postgres): the update is held until you choose Update anyway.
- Release notes for plugins and Unraid OS in the same place, and what changed in Discord.
- Cleanup tab: unused images and leftover containers with a size preview; nothing is removed without confirmation.
- Mobile friendly layout, light/midnight themes, accent colour and custom CSS.
###2026.10.30a
- Dashboard header fix: removed the grey box behind the title and made it less bold (the title no longer picks up Unraid's own heading styles).
- README rewritten to be short: description, features, dashboard screenshot, disclaimer, install and update. Details moved to docs/USAGE.md.
###2026.10.30
- Renamed to Unraid AutoUpdater (plugin name unraid-autoupdater). Existing installs update through a one-time migration that keeps settings, history and the webhook; the old "docker.autoupdate" entry is removed automatically.
- One version everywhere: the plugin version (date based) is the only version shown, on the dashboard, in Discord and in the README.
- New dashboard header: larger logo, bold title and the plugin version in orange.
###2026.10.29a
- Pre-OS maintenance workflow: before an Unraid OS update is installed, plugins (and optionally Docker containers) are updated, the result is verified and the system is re-checked. The OS update only proceeds if the required steps succeeded; optional confirmation step, abort at any time, notifications on the dashboard, Unraid and Discord. Docker updates before the OS are OFF by default.
- The logo is shown beside the title on the dashboard and as the plugin's icon on the Plugins page (installed locally, restored at every boot).
- The Unraid OS tab shows the components that were updated, skipped or failed, and has Confirm / Abort buttons.
###2026.10.29
- Now called "Unraid Auto Updater", release build v1.0.0 (shown in the page, in Discord messages and in the README).
- Unraid OS: automatic install and optional automatic reboot. DEFAULT IS UNCHANGED: check and notify only. Install modes need your explicit confirmation, a maintenance window and a waiting period; stable releases only unless you allow more; a reboot is postponed during a parity check or rebuild; one automatic attempt per version; verified after the reboot.
- Manual "Install update" / "Install and reboot" / "Reboot now" buttons on the Unraid OS tab (with a confirmation).
- Discord messages now use the name "Unraid Auto Updater" and an orange-on-grey icon as avatar and header; you can set your own image URL in Settings.
###2026.10.28f
- Fix: plugin and OS update checks failed to read the version because Unraid prints progress and hook lines around it; the version is now read from the downloaded plugin file.
###2026.10.28e
- Fix: updates now replace the installed files (Unraid only overwrites files that carry a checksum).
###2026.10.28d
- Fix: requests are sent form-encoded (multipart uploads hang on Unraid's web server), which is what kept the page on "Loading".
###2026.10.28c
- Fix: the page stayed on "Loading" because every request must carry Unraid's CSRF token (and Unraid removes it before the plugin sees it).
###2026.10.28b
- Update manager: per-container policies (auto / notify only / ignore), update delay tracked per image digest, maintenance window, critical containers that need your approval.
- Update preview with confirmation before manual (bulk) updates.
- Post-update verification (image, running state, health) with clear results; a container without a health check is not treated as a failure.
- Bounded retries for temporary pull errors only; old image removed only after a verified update (no more broad prune).
- Optional pre-update backups (config / image / appdata) with retention.
- Unraid plugin updates: detection, policies, delay, validation, recovery copy. Automatic installation is OFF by default.
- Unraid OS update detection and notification only (never installs or reboots).
- Discord webhook notifications (test button, per-category and per-type toggles, summary, rate-limit aware).
- New dashboard: overview, Docker table, Plugins table, Unraid OS, Settings, Activity.
- One dispatcher replaces one cron line per schedule; history, statistics, rotated log, export/import of settings.
- Settings from earlier versions are migrated automatically (a backup config.v1.backup.json is kept).
###2026.10.28a
- Per-container schedules (Daily / Weekly / Bi-weekly / Monthly) with the global schedule as the default.
- Per-container notification toggle, one notification per container update.
- Dark grey UI matching the Unraid theme.
- Plugin icon on the Plugins page now opens the settings page; update check via GitHub.
###2026.10.28
- Initial release.
</CHANGES>

